    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδέμω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wall up</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς διασφάγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.117
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>build in</i> a place, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς μέν οἱ πολίων ἑκατοντάδες
					ἐνδέδμηνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.82
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <i>build</i> or <i>make for oneself in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοῖτον θάμνῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					419
				</span></i>
			.</div>
